## Configuration

Add this to the host `application.yml` (the tool never edits it):

```yaml
app:
  query:
    {{id}}:
      enabled: true
      root-dir: ./data/{{id}}
      index-name: {{id}}
      watch-enabled: false
```

{{#if settings}}
> **Warning:** `--settings` adds a `QueryIndexSettings` provider.
> `IndexSettingsController` selects the **first** provider
> (`IndexSettingsController.java:25-31`). Currently Lucene wins because
> `LuceneQueryConfig` has `@Order(0)` (`LuceneQueryConfig.java:16`), but bean
> ordering is not a stable contract, so a default-enabled generated provider
> could take over if ordering changes. Set `enabled=false` on one of them to be
> safe.
{{/if}}
## Build

### Standalone mode

When `../../pom.xml` is absent, Maven resolves the parent from the local
repository. Install the pinned parent and SDK once from a dicoogle-next
checkout:

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -N install
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl dicoogle-next-sdk -am install
```

Then build this module:

```bash
mvn -B -ntp spotless:check test
```

### In-repo mode

To build in place under `backend/plugins/{{artifactId}}`, add the module to
`backend/pom.xml` and add the dependency to `backend/dicoogle-next/pom.xml`.
The parent is then resolved from `../../pom.xml`. The tool never edits those
files.

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl plugins/{{artifactId}} -am spotless:check test
```

